{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits","id":1462491,"title":"W20 Totem bonuses and stat limits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-02T16:58:34-07:00","id":1462491,"title":"W20 Totem bonuses and stat limits","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Can Totem granted stats (Attributes or Skills) put a Werewolf above 5 in a trait? If not, what happens with those extra dots?<br /> <br /> (The case comes from someone that has Strength 5 and Brawl 5, with <i>Polar Bear</i> as Totem you get +1 Strength and can get +2 Brawl too).<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T17:32:12-07:00","id":1462495,"title":"","content":"There's never been a good answer to this from the devs.<br /> <br /> The Totem write-ups have (for multiple editions) been a mess. You have two effective choices: treat the phrasing differences as meaningful and carefully parse each Totem carefully (+2 Subterfuge means your Subterfuge is actually higher for any rolls with a difficulty based on your Subterfuge rating, vs. +2 dice to Subterfuge which means your Subterfuge is still X, but you get two dice when rolling it), or treat it as writers trying to avoid sounding repetitive and use consistent applications.<br /> <br /> Both options are going to run into official rules that don't seem right, which is part of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T23:42:27-07:00","id":1462520,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms is right about the write-ups being a mess. I never thought +2 Subterfuge to be a increase in difficulty though. Because: I general the bonuses aren't given &quot;per character&quot; but &quot;per pack&quot;. Meaning, that you should grant the bonuses to characters from the pack as the pack sees fit, and reassign them on a turn-to-turn basis if necessary. You explicitly can overspend on Totem background to get additional features and 3 dots in Totem more than the base cost is effectively that the totems &quot;powers&quot; are granted to another pack member.<br /> <br /> What isn't clear, but I usually was assumed, is that the bonuses can be split. So, I usually allow for bonuses to increase ratings above 5, but even if I didn't then the bonus of +2 Subterfuge would be two dots, to be divided within the pack, imo.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, you could make it differently and still be within a reasonably valid interpretation of what one can read in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:29:49-07:00","id":1462679,"title":"","content":"I think in one of the editions it specifically says Fenris grants +1 Physical attribute and that it can increase the attribute to 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:49:52-07:00","id":1462685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462679#post1462679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in one of the editions it specifically says Fenris grants +1 Physical attribute and that it can increase the attribute to 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, problem is, that we don't know it this is meant to be a special feature, or is something that other Totems do too. Especially those published later, after the authors might have thought that Fenris would have set the precedence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T13:14:00-07:00","id":1462699,"title":"","content":"On my game Totems are the only thing that would allow attributes or skill to go over 5. Since it's a bonus directly fueled by a spirit it felt right to me that it would not be limited by &quot;mundane&quot; limitations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T13:37:40-07:00","id":1462703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462699#post1462699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my game Totems are the only thing that would allow attributes or skill to go over 5. Since it's a bonus directly fueled by a spirit it felt right to me that it would not be limited by &quot;mundane&quot; limitations</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take it that you meant Totems and Forms, or you really limit Chrinos to 5 Strength?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T13:47:23-07:00","id":1462707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462703#post1462703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take it that you meant Totems and Forms, or you really limit Crinos to 5 Strength?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYep, that and forms. What's already here for stats going over 5 I didn't touch, the Totem one was the one I decided to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8944,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","user":"Tanakyelle","date":". 10-04-2021, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T15:57:18-07:00","id":1462725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462699#post1462699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my game Totems are the only thing that would allow attributes or skill to go over 5. Since it's a bonus directly fueled by a spirit it felt right to me that it would not be limited by &quot;mundane&quot; limitations</div> </div> </div> </div>But is a rating of 5 really the mundane limit?<br /> Or is it the limit a human can achieve in a lifetime?<br /> <br /> I totally allow bonuses from Merits to be added to the ability rating after the dots bought with experience are counted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T16:10:30-07:00","id":1462728,"title":"","content":"Without magic I think it is indeed a true limit. There is only so much you can do with your body and only so much you can know to the point of it giving you more dice.<br /> <br /> It isn't to say that you can't learn more about a subject or develop more of a skill than the &quot;floor&quot; of the 5th dot, but at this point learning more isn't giving you &quot;more dice&quot; to solve problems, which is just one particular aspect of this knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T18:37:51-07:00","id":1462747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462520#post1462520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What isn't clear, but I usually was assumed, is that the bonuses can be split.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can not be split on W20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rage Across the World p. 29</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unlike pack totems, sept totems can divide their bonus dice up among packs</b>. For example, as a sept totem, Boar grants every Garou in the sept a dot of Stamina, and can furthermore grant a single pack two dots of Brawl, or two different packs one dot of Brawl each.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462699#post1462699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my game Totems are the only thing that would allow attributes or skill to go over 5. Since it's a bonus directly fueled by a spirit it felt right to me that it would not be limited by &quot;mundane&quot; limitations</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Fetishes are explicit on allowing extra dots, like <b>Favour of Fenris</b>, it grants +2 to an attribute if your value is 5 currently.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T01:12:28-07:00","id":1462778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462747#post1462747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can not be split on W20:</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. W20 actually states so directly on page 372.<br /> <br /> I'll try to remember that as something W20 made clearer than previous editions...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T02:08:47-07:00","id":1462783,"title":"","content":"I too consider it as a mundane limit, which for a normal human would take a lifetime so both! But yeah I like the idea that going over 5 is when the &quot;magic&quot; happen that's why I decided that bonuses provided by Totems would always allow to go above 5, not only when specified.<br /> <br /> It's fair to allow merits and such to go over, maybe a little bit too &quot;easy&quot; for my taste, but I think it really is a matter of preference at the end of the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T02:19:40-07:00","id":1462785,"title":"","content":"Really, being able to get to 6 in an Attribute isn't the end of the world. The bigger concern is whatever broken combos you can slap together via Totems, Gifts, Fetishes, Rites, and so on as there's no anti-stacking rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T04:56:52-07:00","id":1462791,"title":"","content":"Back in 2nd Edition &quot;Mothers Touch&quot; was rolled with Medicine and Unicorn gave +2 Medicine and +3 to Gifts involving certain aspects, including healing. So, Mother's Touch was +5 dice to begin with... Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T08:42:40-07:00","id":1462801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462785#post1462785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, being able to get to 6 in an Attribute isn't the end of the world. The bigger concern is whatever broken combos you can slap together via Totems, Gifts, Fetishes, Rites, and so on as there's no anti-stacking rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with stacking I particularly find that combos aren't necessarily the end of the world. An elder vampire with Str 6 + Pot 6 have effective 12 Strength before adding further shenanigans and can make half of those be automatic successes in any Str related action, and this isn't exactly a combo. Garou will fight things that go from that to worse and their magic is good, but not the most stellar in the WoD, so they need their main assets well sharped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T13:41:22-07:00","id":1462832,"title":"","content":"I once made a Garou without even trying to cheese that could do 18 A damage minimum per hit pre-soak (that's levels of damage, not dice of damage). The most powerful thing involved was a level 3 Gift. A Gen 7 vampire with Stamina 6/Fortitude 6 would need to roll perfect 100% successes (even using the DAV20 rules that let Fortitude work like Potence for autosoak, the remaining dice still need to roll perfect) or die. So that's with me rolling zero successes on my remaining damage dice, and them rolling all successes on their soak.<br /> <br /> And there's a lot out there in WtA that could have made that an even more potent combo. I'm pretty sure I could get it up to 26 min. damage with more Fetishes and Totem bonuses, and with a certain level 5 Gift take my Gnosis one-shot monster and be able to start using Rage with it.<br /> <br /> Yes, WtA has a lot of really tough opponents to challenge how much punch the Garou can toss around, but even then very little is calibrated for that sort of stacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T15:37:52-07:00","id":1462841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462832#post1462832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once made a Garou without even trying to cheese that could do 18 A damage minimum per hit pre-soak (that's levels of damage, not dice of damage). The most powerful thing involved was a level 3 Gift. A Gen 7 vampire with Stamina 6/Fortitude 6 would need to roll perfect 100% successes (even using the DAV20 rules that let Fortitude work like Potence for autosoak, the remaining dice still need to roll perfect) or die. So that's with me rolling zero successes on my remaining damage dice, and them rolling all successes on their soak.<br /> <br /> And there's a lot out there in WtA that could have made that an even more potent combo. I'm pretty sure I could get it up to 26 min. damage with more Fetishes and Totem bonuses, and with a certain level 5 Gift take my Gnosis one-shot monster and be able to start using Rage with it.<br /> <br /> Yes, WtA has a lot of really tough opponents to challenge how much punch the Garou can toss around, but even then very little is calibrated for that sort of stacking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking along those lines, but the problem with Garou is that while you can stack damage dice absurdly (see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack?p=1442413#post1442413\">this post</a>), there are not many ways to hit more accurately. Making <i>A LOT</i> of theoretical optimization, I can get between 22 and 44 automatic damage per hit, but at most 13 dice at difficulty 3 to hit.<br /> <br /> Compare those vs a Vampire with Celerity 5, Dexterity 5 and Athletics 5; not amazing by vampire standards, but that is a 15 dice dodging pool (more if the vampire pumps blood for Dexterity); and it gets to be a larger pool the better Generation it has.<br /> <br /> <br /> After a point damage dice are not the difference as nearly everything would be killed on one hit (or several Rage-enabled hits), but some high powered creatures are virtually untouchable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I would like to share my optimized starting Metis, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\"><b>Ugly McAngry</b></a>, that has 24 damage dice vs Wyrm creatures","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-09-2021, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T16:42:23-07:00","id":1462844,"title":"","content":"That diff 3 part is really huge in the system math though. 13 dice to attack at diff 3 needs to be contested by 22 dice to dodge at diff 6 for the defender to have the edge (and 21-22 dice is still coin-flip territory).<br /> <br /> One of the places where vampires suffers the most in crossovers (though spirits when just keeping things to WtA don't do well in this regard either) is a lack of ways to get difficulty modifiers in their favor compared to a lot of other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T19:53:30-07:00","id":1462853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462491-w20-totem-bonuses-and-stat-limits?p=1462844#post1462844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the places where vampires suffers the most in crossovers (though spirits when just keeping things to WtA don't do well in this regard either) is a lack of ways to get difficulty modifiers in their favor compared to a lot of other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite true, and a serious oversight in WoD that they finally addressed in V5. It took what, only 27 years? The rules on diff are too inconsistent from a line to the other, and even in the same line they're frequently less visible but far more cheesy than bonus dice.<br /> <br /> Stacking bonuses, difficulty shenanigans and multiple actions. WoD have been for decades extremely keen on ignoring glaring rule issues and insist in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:08:36-07:00","id":1462857,"title":"","content":"WW fixed a lot of it in 1997 with Aeon/Trinity and the games built off it, which helped inspire further fixes in 2004 via the nWoD launch.<br /> <br /> And we haven't actually seen if W5 will make sure there's better consistency or not to know if it's actually fixed for the main cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T20:48:53-07:00","id":1462865,"title":"","content":"Oh, I was just talking about the difficulty, the other messes we still have to wait and see.<br /> <br /> But my problem is precisely that the bugs are so glaring that they went through new editions of WoD and never addressed them. And other games from WW showed precisely that they could solve the mess but simply didn't wanted to.<br /> <br /> Which is comprehensible from the perspective that they wanted to avoid saying that mechanics from old supplements couldn't be used in the new edition, but I really can't force myself to forgive them about this, they should have fixed it no later than Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T22:37:07-07:00","id":1462873,"title":"","content":"Well, many times in a row now, things suffer because Vampire went first (not that it's something wrong with vampires). VtM Rev. was in development at the same time as Aeon, so by the time the lessons of Aeon were there to learn, Rev. was already set as being closer to WoD 2e and the rest of the Rev. games had to follow suit. V20 started as a one-off nostalgia omnibus for old school fans, and wasn't intended to be a rules update or to kick off a whole new edition, which the rest of the 20th books continued to follow suit.<br /> <br /> I just think it's kind of unfair to discount the nWoD 1e books here, simply because one of the whole points was to be able to fix bugs in the systems that kept getting maintained because of continuity; even V5 has some funky rules that are only there because of continuity (having Generation and Blood Potency as a prime example).<br /> <br /> Hopefully, getting back to the main topic, one of the things W5 does take from Forsaken, is just having Totem creation rules (which completely avoid the stacking issue) so that you don't have to try to figure out authorial intent by parsing phrasing. I've tried a half dozen times to make WtA Totem creation rules that even come close to keeping the 1e to W20 Totem costs, and it never works well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T23:12:03-07:00","id":1462876,"title":"","content":"I'm discounting nWoD because it was another game, like it or not, and as much as it wanted to be a successor it was from the beginning leaning on different themes. It isn't to say it is bad, I actually enjoy playing CoD as much as I enjoy discussing cWoD and despite CoD 2nd ed being far better we can't ignore the role of 1st edition on it becoming its own thing.<br /> <br /> But I guess that totem creation rules are something to hope for. I still have to play test V5's rules (my players are real grognards in every RPG we play...), although they seem to fare far better than the setting so I guess it isn't unreasonable to expect such rules. But then, they'll also have to keep continuity, as whatever they are they'll have to port many classic totems.<br /> <br /> To be honest about making an adequate interpretation of WtA's totems, I think there are only two sensible strategies: make a ruling on the spot and see if it works, or ignore the current stats completely and build (mechanically) from scratch, so you can be consistent on your own game. Trying to make a general rule is just more work than it is worth.<br /> <br /> You don't have to make every totem again to build them from scratch. Just take notes on how you'll approach this and present the players with the <i>ideas</i> of the totems, so you only have to build what you'll use, when you'll use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}